447 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 448 0 R>>/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/DA(0 0 0 rg /Helv 8.6 Tf)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 8392704/M(D:20250930131256-06'00')/MK<<>>/NM(401dd15e-4d9b-4545-bcf8-cc1eced1efe4)/Rect[66.1431 52.843507 567.267 446.829]/T(Text Field49)/V(On 05Oct26, the sample vials for ETX-261002-0288 were retrieved from controlled refrigerated storage and transferred into the sterile microbiology laboratory suites. In accordance with standard operating procedures, container surfaces were sprayed with acidified bleach disinfectant, placed into pre-disinfected transfer bins, and allowed a verified 10-minute contact time. Secondary surface disinfection with acidified bleach was conducted in the ISO 8 anteroom 114 prior to entering cleanroom 114B. Inside ISO 7 cleanroom 114B, processing analyst Alex Saravia \(ES\) executed a final disinfection step before introducing the containers into the ISO 5 BSC E001316. Direct inoculation was performed by adding 15 mL of sample \(divided across ten 3 mL vials\) along with 3 mL of sterile Tween 80 into 300 mL of Fluid Thioglycollate Medium \(FTM\) and 300 mL of Tryptic Soy Broth \(TSB\) in accordance with method suitability study ETX-250826-0390. A matching negative control jar with identical modifications was prepared concurrently and handled identically. Following inoculation, media bottles were transferred into calibrated incubators to commence incubation.)>>
endobj

