476 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 477 0 R>>/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/DA(0 0 0 rg /Helv 8.5 Tf)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 8392704/M(D:20250930131345-06'00')/MK<<>>/NM(1a940318-0f35-48e4-8311-69dfeb8caf9f)/Rect[66.1431 52.174684 567.936 567.901]/T(Text Field51)/V(A thorough review of testing records, training files, and equipment documentation confirmed that all analysts involved in sample preparation, processing, aliquoting, and instrument reading were fully trained and qualified in accordance with MICRO-SOP-44. Comprehensive interviews conducted with prepping analyst Mukyung Jang \(MJ\), processing analyst Alex Saravia \(ES\), and aliquoting/reading analyst Cuong Du \(CCD\) confirmed strict adherence to aseptic technique, proper gowning procedures, and standard operating protocols throughout all handling steps. No procedural anomalies, technique compromises, spills, or unusual occurrences were identified during any phase of testing.\n\nAnalyzing a 6-month sample history for Optimal Balance Pharmacy, this specific analyte "TESAMORELIN 8 MG/ML \(3 ML\) Injection" has had no prior Out-of-Specification \(OOS\) occurrences under Celsis Sterility Testing.\n\nUpon review of the environmental monitoring data, absence of microbial recovery \(No Growth\) was demonstrated across all critical ISO 5 zones and personnel monitoring on the date of testing.\n\nPersonnel environmental monitoring performed on 05Oct26 for processing analyst Alex Saravia \(ES\) and on 12Oct26 for aliquoting analyst Cuong Du \(CCD\) demonstrated No Growth across all touch plates. Daily surface and settling plate monitoring of ISO 5 BSC E001316 \(used for processing on 05Oct26\) and ISO 5 BSC E001798 \(used for aliquoting on 12Oct26\) yielded No Growth across all locations. Weekly active air and surface monitoring performed on 05Oct26 across Cleanroom Suite 114 also demonstrated No Growth.\n\nDuring weekly active air monitoring performed on 12Oct26 across Cleanroom Suite 114, recovery of 6 CFUs was observed on an active air plate located in ISO 8 Anteroom 114 \(ETX-261021-0578\). Confirmatory identification of these isolates identified Moraxella osloensis, Sporisorium graminicola, Staphylococcus haemolyticus, Staphylococcus hominis, Kocuria indica, Ustilago maydis, and Kocuria rhizophila. Importantly, none of the isolates recovered from the ISO 8 anteroom active air plate matched Bacillus paralicheniformis, the Gram-positive rod recovered from the failing FTM sample. Furthermore, weekly surface monitoring of Cleanroom Suite 114 performed concurrently on 12Oct26 demonstrated No Growth.\n\nMonthly cleaning and disinfection of cleanrooms \(ISO 7/8\) and biological safety cabinets \(ISO 5\) were performed per MICRO-SOP-9, with all chemical indicators passing, confirming that environmental sanitization remained validated and in control.\n\nIn conclusion, comprehensive investigation into the testing process, equipment, media, personnel technique, environmental monitoring, and sample history identified no laboratory error or testing aberration contributing to the elevated luminescence result. Phase I laboratory investigation confirms that the positive Celsis Sterility Test result is valid. Per laboratory procedures, Phase II investigation is initiated to evaluate client manufacturing and formulation factors.)>>
endobj

